    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Apply a lyrics animation resource to recognized lyrics in the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --resource TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Lyrics animation resource: vimo://<id>\r\n          --cover-old         Cover existing lyrics animation results\r\n          --language TEXT     Lyrics language, e.g. zh-CN or en-US\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nNOTE: configure a non-zero draft canvas first, for example with `draft config --ratio 16:9`.\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Apply a lyrics animation resource to the current lyrics result\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft lyrics animation add --resource vimo://123\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Apply a lyrics animation resource to recognized lyrics in the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --resource TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Lyrics animation resource: vimo://<id>\r\n          --cover-old         Cover existing lyrics animation results\r\n          --language TEXT     Lyrics language, e.g. zh-CN or en-US\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nNOTE: configure a non-zero draft canvas first, for example with `draft config --ratio 16:9`.\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Apply a lyrics animation resource to the current lyrics result\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft lyrics animation add --resource vimo://123\r\n",
